/-!
# Second-normalizer exclusion for M₂₂, 3.M₂₂, M₂₃ and HS

The original PSL₂ section forces field four. The natural plane map, with
kernel exactly C_V(L), bounds the dimension of the entire original V₂ by
six. Each actual quotient carrier has central quotient of order divisible
by eleven. For the centerless carriers, cubic rank two and the ambient SQTK
hypothesis supply quasisimplicity from the containing C-component; the
three-cover already carries its precise quasisimple marking.

A perfect group with such a two-core quotient is generated by its
11-elements: the prime-to-eleven residual has noncentral normal image in
the quasisimple quotient, hence full image, and perfectness kills the
remaining two-group quotient. A binary action below dimension ten has
image of order prime to eleven, so it is trivial. Applied to K on full V₂,
this contradicts the original natural L₂ action. No faithfulness assumption
on K and no irreducibility assumption on the central cover are used.

The preceding literal quotient model and natural-cover maps belong to
qt-d-1222-natural-flag-cartan and are ultimately discharged by
qt-d-1222-natural-local-geometry. This module discharges the owned second
refinement in these four carrier branches. The relative-components owner
retains the other branches and the field-four triangle.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith 11.0.3, 11.1.1--11.1.2 and G.7.1,
printed pp.760--765,347, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004.
-/

